; modules/generated's codegen rule references ../../proto/ecommerce.proto —
; a path outside this project's own root, which is both outside the Docker
; build context (scoped to just backend-ocaml/, not the repo root where
; proto/ actually lives) and outside dune's own project-root sandboxing for
; (deps ...) stanzas. Nothing in bin/dune or any other module here actually
; depends on the ecommerce_generated library, so excluding this directory
; entirely doesn't remove anything real from the build — it's still there,
; documented as future codegen wiring (see docs/grpc-coverage.md), just not
; unconditionally attempted by every default `dune build`.
(subdir modules (dirs :standard \ generated))
